window.docContents[163].resolve({"/Encapsulation/Static-classes-and-namespaces/#Core-C______--Encapsulation--Static-classes-and-namespaces":{"contents":"Neither  nor  carries types, and the rules MethodCall and Delete need the static class of the receiver.After a program is checked, annotate walks it with the typing context. It writes into every method call and every delete the class the receiver has in . It also rewrites an unqualified m(args) inside a member body into this->m(args).A program runs only when it parses, type checks and annotates. The function prepare checks the program and annotates it. A program that check rejects stops with its type error. A failure of annotate on a program that check accepts is an error of the implementation, and the program stops too.\n\nA namespace N { … } holds classes, class templates and namespaces, and the parser flattens it. Every class and class template declared inside is named N::C, and the parser reads every unqualified class name in a type or in new inside the namespace as N::C. The type parameter of a class template is the exception. Its name belongs to the template declaration, not to the namespace (N4659 §6.3.9 ¶2), so T inside namespace N { template<typename T> class C { … }; } stays T. Outside the namespace the class has its qualified name, N::C, in types and in new. Namespaces add no rule of typing or of evaluation.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Encapsulation","header":"6.4. Static classes and namespaces","id":"/Encapsulation/Static-classes-and-namespaces/#Core-C______--Encapsulation--Static-classes-and-namespaces"}});